Digital Grocery Store

1. Project Overview

For this project I designed a Digital Grocery Store. IT is a three-page website that creates a small online grocery shopping experience. The first page shows different food items on supermarket shelves, the second page shows the items inside a shopping cart, and the last page is a receipt showing the items, quantities, and prices.

I mainly used HTML and CSS to build the website. I used CSS Grid differently on each page to organize the images and create the layouts. I also used links between the HTML pages so users can move through the store, cart, and receipt by clicking on buttons.

The project includes three HTML files (index.html, page2.html, and page3.html), one CSS file (style.css), and an images folder containing the food images and background images.


2. AI Tools or Other Resources

I used AI during this project for image generation. I used it to generate the three supermarket background images, so the store shelf, shopping cart, and receipt could have a similar visual style.

Some example prompts I used for image generation were:
- "Generate a colorful cartoon-style supermarket with empty shelves so I can add my own grocery items."
- "Create a supermarket shopping cart background in the same style, with a large empty cart in the center."
- "Create a vertical supermarket receipt background with a large blank receipt in the center."

I also used AI to debug some problems that came up while coding:
- "Why does my background image get cropped when I use `background-size: cover`?"
- "How can I make a long vertical background image scroll instead of fitting it into one screen?"
- "Why does changing `grid-column` move my image too far, and how can I make smaller position adjustments?"
- "How can I keep a navigation button fixed in the corner while the page scrolls?"
